  "title": "Aisha bint Abi Bakr",
  "summary": "Aisha bint Abi Bakr, born in Mecca around 613 or 614, is recorded as married to Muhammad in Medina in 624 (one source says 623 or 624). Muhammad died in May 632 at her dwelling. She is linked to the Battle of the Camel of 656, named for the camel she rode, and afterwards retired to Medina, where she died in 678. The pin marks Medina.",
